      "text": "Let the cost of each pen be $p$ cents and the cost of each pencil be $c$ cents. The given equations can then be written as\n\\[4p+3c=224,\\quad 2p+5c=154.\\]Multiply both sides of the second equation by $1.5$ to get\n\\[3p+p+7.5c=231.\\]This yields $p=$ 7 cents. Plugging that into the second equation gives\n\\[14c=154-3(7)=122,\\]so $c=\\boxed{9}$ cents.The answer is: 9",
